1. Inter-VLAN Routing Operation
  - VLANs are used to segment switched Layer 2 networks for a variety of reasons.
  - Hosts in a one VLAN cannot communicate with hosts in another VLAN unless there is a router or a Layer 3 switch to provide routing services.
  - Inter-VLAN routing is the process of forwarding network traffic from one VLAN to another VLAN.
  - Inter-VLAN routing options:
    a. Legacy Inter-VLAN routing
    b. Router-on-a-Stick
    c. Layer 3 switch using switched virtual interfaces

2. Router-on-a-Stick Inter-VLAN Routing
  - How traffic from 2 different VLANs communicate with each other through physical cable between Layer 2 switch and router 
  - PC VLAN 10 -> Router -> PC VLAN 30
  - Does not scale beond 50 VLANs
  - Apabila PC dalam VLAN 10 nak hantar data ke PC dalam VLAN 20:
    a. Dari Switch ke Router (Naik ke atas):
        Switch terima frame daripada PC VLAN 10, lekatkan 802.1Q tag (VLAN 10), dan hantar melalui port trunk menuju ke router.   
    b. Router Terima & Proses (Layer 3 Routing):
        Port fizikal router terima frame tersebut, baca tag VLAN 10, dan serahkan kepada subinterface G0/0.10 (yang menjadi Default Gateway bagi VLAN 10). Router buka lapisan IP, tengok alamat IP destinasi (yang berada dalam subnet VLAN 20), dan buat keputusan routing.   
    c. Dari Router Balik ke Switch (Turun ke bawah):
        Router buang tag VLAN 10, lekatkan 802.1Q tag baharu (VLAN 20) melalui subinterface G0/0.20, dan hantar semula keluar melalui kabel fizikal yang sama balik ke switch.   
    d. Switch Hantar ke Destinasi:
        Switch terima frame bertag VLAN 20 tadi, buang tag tersebut, dan hantar ke PC destinasi dalam VLAN 20
